==============================================================================
A7. Pillai censuses in wider boxes
==============================================================================
|2^a - 10^b| <= 100, 0 <= a <= 300, 0 <= b <= 90: 23 solutions; with a, b >= 1: 14; largest b: 3; largest a: 10
|2^K - 3^L| <= 100, 1 <= K <= 700, 1 <= L <= 400: 26 solutions (lane box K<=200, L<=130 had 26); largest L: 5; NEITHER: 15; tier-C: 6
for L <= 400, |Delta| <= 100 forces K <= 634 < 700, so this list is complete for ALL K and all L <= 400 (FINITE-EXACT);
  beyond that, 100 <= 3^L/(4L) for every L >= 8, so any further solution would be in tier A and sit on a convergent
  multiple (PROVED via Legendre); no elementary bound on L follows, which is why the full list stays CITED context.
